From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:12:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winemetal: Load the MetalFX presenter when asked.

MacNeutron's MetalFX presenter (libmacneutron-present.dylib) used to be
injected into a game's Wine processes with DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES. Wine's
loader in wine.app is signed with the hardened runtime, which ignores
DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES, so the presenter now ships beside winemetal.so
and winemetal.so loads it itself: a constructor dlopens
@loader_path/libmacneutron-present.dylib when MACNEUTRON_PRESENT is 1,
and prints one line to stderr if that fails. Nothing changes when the
variable is unset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c b/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c
index 6aba678..0a72cc3 100644
--- a/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c
+++ b/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c
@@ -3267,6 +3267,16 @@ _MTLTexture_getBytes(void *obj) {
   return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
 
+/* MacNeutron's MetalFX presenter, from beside this library, when the launcher asks for it (MACNEUTRON_PRESENT=1).
+ * Wine's loader runs under the hardened runtime, which ignores DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES, so winemetal.so loads it here,
+ * once in each process that loads winemetal.dll. */
+__attribute__((constructor)) static void
+load_presenter(void) {
+  const char *p = getenv("MACNEUTRON_PRESENT");
+  if (p && !strcmp(p, "1") && !dlopen("@loader_path/libmacneutron-present.dylib", RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL))
+    fprintf(stderr, "winemetal: can't load the MetalFX presenter: %s\n", dlerror());
+}
+
 /*
  * Definition from cache.c
  */
